
# Backend REST tests for VS Code REST Client (or similar)
# Usage:
# 1) Démarrez le serveur : `cd backend && npm run dev`
# 2) (Optionnel) Créez un user test admin : `npm run seed:test` (ou `ts-node src/scripts/create-test-user.ts`)
# 3) Lancez chaque requête ci-dessous dans l'éditeur REST Client. Copiez le token retourné par `/auth/login`
#    et remplacez `{{TOKEN}}` dans les requêtes suivantes.

@TOKEN = <PASTE_YOUR_JWT_HERE>


### Register (create a new intervenant)
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"email": "resttest+1@example.com",
	"mot_de_passe": "TestPass123!",
	"nom": "Rest",
	"prenom": "Tester"
}


### Login (get JWT)
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"email": "resttest+1@example.com",
	"mot_de_passe": "TestPass123!"
}

# -> Copy the `token` value from the response and use it in subsequent requests as `{{TOKEN}}`


### Profile (requires Authorization header)
GET http://localhost:3000/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN}}


### Admin: list intervenants (requires admin token)
GET http://localhost:3000/admin/intervenants
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN}}


### Admin: get single intervenant (replace :id)
GET http://localhost:3000/admin/intervenants/1
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN}}


### Admin: change password for intervenant (replace :id)
POST http://localhost:3000/admin/intervenants/1/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"new_password": "NewSecret123!"
}


### Admin: delete intervenant (replace :id)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/admin/intervenants/1
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN}}

